      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Inception (2010) revolutionized modern sci-fi by masterfully weaving dreams within dreams. Christopher Nolan's labyrinthine heist film follows Dom Cobb (Leonardo DiCaprio) through increasingly complex layers of subconscious architecture, setting new standards for practical effects and narrative complexity. The film's influence echoes through later mind-bending works like <a href=\"/movie/45612\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"45612\">Source Code</a> (2011) and <a href=\"/movie/284052\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"284052\">Doctor Strange</a> (2016). Its practical effects, including the rotating hallway sequence, proved audiences still crave practical over CGI spectacle, influencing <a href=\"/movie/353081\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"353081\">Mission: Impossible - Fallout</a> (2018) and <a href=\"/movie/577922\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"577922\">Tenet</a> (2020)."
      },
