      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's architectural impossibilities, designed by production designer Guy Hendrix Dyas, drew from artists like M.C. Escher and the paradoxical structures of <a href=\"/movie/2654\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2654\">In the Mouth of Madness</a> (1994). This visual vocabulary influenced later films like <a href=\"/movie/157336\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"157336\">Interstellar</a> (2014) and <a href=\"/movie/438631\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"438631\">Dune</a> (2021). The practical effects work, particularly the zero-gravity hotel sequence, raised the bar for in-camera effects, proving audiences appreciate real stunts over CGI."
      }
